        "response": "I've found the relevant data in the workspace. Here's what I found for the **Everyday Crew Tee** price comparison:\n\nFrom the `state_cs_products` table (the customer-support product catalog):\n\n| Detail | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Product ID** | CS-PROD-001 |\n| **Product Name** | Everyday Crew Tee |\n| **Current Price** | **$24.99** |\n| **Original Price** | **$29.99** |\n| **Category** | Apparel \u2192 T-Shirts |\n| **Stock** | In stock (150 units) |\n| **Return Window** | 30 days |\n\nAnd from the `state_cs_order_items` table, there's an existing order for this product:\n\n| Order Detail | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Order ID** | CS-ORD-001 |\n| **Customer** | CUST-001 (Alice Smith, Gold tier) |\n| **Item ID** | CS-ITEM-001 |\n| **Variant** | Blue / M |\n| **Quantity** | 2 |\n| **Price Paid (per unit)** | **$29.99** |\n| **Order Total for Tees** | $59.98 |\n| **Order Status** | Delivered |\n\n### Price Comparison Summary\n\nThe Everyday Crew Tee has **dropped in price by $5.00 per unit** since the order was placed:\n- **Paid:** $29.99/each \u2192 $59.98 total (2 units)\n- **Current price:** $24.99/each \u2192 $49.98 total\n- **Difference:** **$5.00 per unit / $10.00 total**\n\nWould you like me to look into a **price match** or **price adjustment** for this order? I can check the company's price match policy and process a refund for the difference if eligible. Just let me know your customer ID (or confirm if you're CUST-001 / Alice Smith) and I'll get started!",
